{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ATTESTATION STALENESS — a scheduling lesson, measured not assumed.\n\nAfter landing the 1484 split (HEAD 96d683a0d -> e1566b5f4), ALL THREE outstanding attestations went\nstale at once, and for TWO DIFFERENT reasons:\n\n  f844: stale-head       (signed at 96d683a0d, HEAD is now e1566b5f4)\n  a574: stale-head       (same)\n  eb58: stale-pin-drift  ('reviewed related-ticket material is stale')\n\nThe first two are the documented moving-base-ref effect: LANDING A COMMIT SILENTLY INVALIDATES EVERY\nOUTSTANDING ATTESTATION IN THE WORKTREE. Cheap to detect with 'review-plan <id> --status --ref HEAD'\n(read-only, no LLM) — do that BEFORE assuming a ticket is still claimable, not after a failed claim.\n\nThe eb58 case is the more useful one. It went stale-PIN-DRIFT, not stale-head, because I edited its\nCHILD cb6f (pushing the parent's uncovered ACs down) AFTER eb58's review had already passed and been\nsigned. A review pins its direct dependencies' material; changing a child invalidates the parent.\n\nSCHEDULING CONSEQUENCE, now being followed: do NOT re-review eb58 yet. Every remaining child edit\n(cb6f, 172e, 7761, cc33, d23e each still need their own plan reviews and will very likely be edited\nin remediation) will re-staleen the parent. Re-reviewing it now buys an attestation that the next\nchild edit destroys, at ~14 min of LLM per run. Refresh eb58 ONCE, at close time, after its children\nhave settled. The claim itself already succeeded on the fresh attestation, so nothing is blocked.\n\nCorollary for the remaining epic: each landed change re-staleens everything unclaimed. Batch the\nplan reviews AFTER a landing, not before — and prefer --status (free) over a speculative re-review."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785480128310886001,"uuid":"1f9c5069-65b1-44ef-87f9-5ad81a63ba3e"}